Fleet review 2026-10-06 · kind: bug · confidence: verified

Fixed in 6e91e79 (local main, not pushed). All three from 'Done when': the allocator takes max(counter, highest task id + 1); create writes create-only through a new create_task door and re-allocates on a hit (8 attempts, then dies without writing); pull raises a counter that ends up at or below the highest task id. The pull repair only touches a counter that exists -- a board without one is left without one (t/73, t/99 pin 'a pull changes nothing here'), the allocator floor covers it. Full suite: 3 files red on the first run (t/72 from k323, t/73 and t/99 from the counter being created), all three green after the adjustment.
